## T8 — Durable outbox with ordered automatic delivery
Reasoning: The core of G1: write-before-dispatch, persistence across reload/close, ordered automatic drain meeting D1; 
unknown-outcome recovery follows in T27.
Task: Every eligible text/reply send is written to a per-user IndexedDB outbox (key, conversation, content, reply 
target, requested mention IDs, original send time, window start, order, state, generation) before dispatch and before 
the composer clears; pending items render with a text label; items drain automatically per conversation in order when 
connectivity returns, with ≤ 10 pending and quota available all delivered within 10 s; confirmed items become the 
normal message; the outbox survives reload and tab close; attachments/voice are never queued (Phase 4 behavior kept); 
if the outbox write fails or storage is unavailable, nothing is dispatched and the text and reply stay with the D5 
message.
Done when: AC-001, AC-002, AC-004, AC-011, and AC-039 hold in the real UI, and 10 messages queued offline are 
delivered in order, once each, within 10 s of reconnecting.
Verify by: New E2E specs for those ACs plus the 10-message D1 timing case (offline context, reload offline, tab close, 
IndexedDB disabled and failing writes) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
Covers: FR-001, FR-002, FR-003, FR-010, FR-033, BR-002, BR-003, AC-001, AC-002, AC-004, AC-011, AC-039
Root: T8
Depends on: T7

## T27 — Unknown-outcome recovery through the fence
Reasoning: Review r1 #3, #14: fenced recovery is a separate failure surface from durable enqueue, and AC-040 needs it.
Task: An attempt that ends without a usable response (network error after dispatch, timeout, 5xx after reaching the 
server, tab closed mid-request) leaves the item unknown; before any cancel, expiry, or redispatch the app fences it 
under a new generation; a stored result resolves as delivered (never cancelled or expired); a not-stored result only 
permits the transition that was requested — cancel and expiry complete without any create, and redispatch happens only 
while the item is still current, eligible, and inside its delivery window; cancel is offered only for items known not 
stored; a fence answered 403 `NOT_PARTICIPANT` (access lost while the item was unknown) makes the item failed per 
BR-005 with its text kept, stops automatic attempts, and is never treated as not stored (no expiry, no cancel) — 
"Tentar de novo" fences under a new generation first, so a stored result resolves as delivered and a not-stored result 
follows the normal rules, and "Apagar" only removes the local item.
Done when: AC-003, AC-038, AC-040, AC-042, and the AC-046 5xx clause hold in the real UI with real routes, an unknown 
item fenced as not stored after its 24 h window expires without any create request, and an unknown item whose fence 
returns 403 is failed (not expired, not delivered, not re-created) for both a committed-but-response-lost message and 
a not-yet-stored one.
Verify by: New E2E specs (network error after dispatch, dropped response after pass-through, gateway 5xx after 
pass-through, held create + tab close + reopen, stored-but-unknown item at cancel and at 24 h, unknown-but-not-stored 
item at 24 h, via test clock; removal from the room before fencing for a committed-response-lost item and a 
not-yet-stored item, then access restored and "Tentar de novo" → delivered once / sent once) pass 3 consecutive runs 
in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
Covers: FR-005, FR-006, FR-009, BR-005, BR-007, AC-003, AC-038, AC-040, AC-042, AC-046
Root: T27
Depends on: T8

## T10 — Cross-tab outbox ownership and leases
Reasoning: Multi-tab exactly-once (R1-q16 B) is the riskiest client protocol; proven right after fenced recovery, 
before unrelated features.
Task: All tabs of the same user share the outbox and show each item once; per conversation only the oldest unresolved 
item is eligible and one tab holds an atomic drain claim (lease: request timeout 30 s, lease 45 s) that ends on tab 
close/crash or expiry, after which another tab fences and resumes; when connectivity returns, an attempt started 
before or during the outage is superseded immediately under a new generation without waiting for the timeout or lease; 
no two create requests of one conversation overlap across tabs; cancel is atomic against claims and propagates to 
every tab.
Done when: AC-005, AC-006, AC-041, and the AC-045 E2E cases hold with two real tabs, including an attempt started 
during an active outage delivered within 10 s of recovery.
Verify by: New E2E specs (two tabs, held create, tab close, hung lease, attempt dispatched during outage, simultaneous 
online, cancel/claim race, network-log overlap check) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; regression suites 
pass.
Covers: FR-002, FR-004, FR-005, BR-003, BR-007, AC-005, AC-006, AC-041, AC-045
Root: T10
Depends on: T27

## T9 — Definitive failures, rate-limit retry, and expiry
Reasoning: The user-visible failure states (BR-005 definitive, 429 transient, BR-006 expiry) are a separate outcome 
from unknown recovery.
Task: Definitive rejections show the item failed with its text and "Tentar de novo"/"Apagar" and block only later 
items of that conversation; "Apagar" removes it and the next item proceeds; 409 retry resends the content under a new 
key once; 429 and 401-with-valid-session stay pending and retry automatically in order; items fenced as not stored 24 
h after send become "expirada" without auto-send (a fence answered 403 is a definitive failure, never "not stored" — 
T27); manual retry of an expired item keeps the key and the original send time and opens a new 24 h window under the 
normal rules.
Done when: AC-007, AC-008, AC-009 (drawer clause), AC-010, AC-043, and the AC-046 definitive-class clauses hold, and 
an expired item retried manually keeps its original send time in the outbox.
