## T2 — Server attempt and sender fencing with key correlation  [done]
Plan version: 3
Covers: FR-006, FR-011, FR-034, BR-001, BR-004, BR-005, AC-044, AC-045, AC-046, AC-035
Root: T2
State delta:
- On the LOCAL database (migration `supabase/migrations/20261007095045_message_send_attempt_fencing.sql`, written + 
applied locally, NOT online): keyed creates go through `public.create_message_attempt`, which checks the key's attempt 
row (`private.message_send_attempts`, PK sender/conversation/key) after its INSERT and holds the row lock to commit, 
so a fenced or older generation never commits and at most one message exists per key; `public.fence_message_attempt` 
returns the stored message or records the new generation (lower generations can no longer commit) and never creates a 
message; the Phase 4 RPC `create_message_with_attachments` keeps its signature and delegates to the guarded function.
- Writes outside the fenced contract are refused at the database: `send_message_as_self` requires `client_message_id 
IS NULL` (client keyed inserts denied; unkeyed direct inserts still work); trigger 
`messages_client_message_id_immutable` refuses setting/changing/clearing a key or moving a keyed message to another 
conversation/sender for every role (42501); trigger `messages_keyed_insert_fence` fences raw keyed inserts (e.g. a 
Phase 4 server's service-role insert) — allowed only while the key has no fence state, else ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED — and 
records delivery.
- Every keyed message has a delivery record (backfill for existing keyed messages; fence/replay record untracked ones 
under the key lock); a keyed message deleted after this migration is never re-created (fence → `stored` with `message: 
null`; generation-carrying create → 410 MESSAGE_DELETED).
- `POST /api/messages/create` accepts `attemptGeneration` (≥1, requires key and expectedSenderId) and 
`expectedSenderId` (users.id; mismatch → 403 SENDER_MISMATCH before anything is read/stored/fenced); new `POST 
/api/messages/fence` (own key only; 401 anon; 200 stored|not_stored; 409 ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED for older generations; 403 
NOT_PARTICIPANT; never creates). Create/fence responses carry `clientMessageId` (top level and on `message`). Original 
composition stored per key (content, type, replyToId, sorted attachmentIds) for replay comparison; T4 adds sorted 
mention IDs.
- Status codes: missing conversation 403 NOT_PARTICIPANT (was 404) on create/fence only; non-UUID ids 400 (was 500); 
unchanged keyed replay whose reply target was later deleted → 200 (was 400). Generation-less keyed creates (Phase 4 
client) keep create/replay 200/409 and lose to fence state (D4); unkeyed creates unchanged.
- Files: `src/app/api/messages/create/route.ts`, new `src/app/api/messages/fence/route.ts`, 
`src/lib/auth/authorize.ts` (expectedSenderId and missingConversationAsNotParticipant options; other routes keep 404), 
`src/lib/auth/rate-limit.ts` (new fail-open 'message:fence' 60/min), repositories and interfaces, new 
`src/lib/messaging/message-attempts.ts`, `src/lib/messaging/message-composition.ts`, 
`src/repositories/implementations/supabase/message-attempt-rpc.ts`, `src/types/messaging.ts` (Message.clientMessageId, 
attempt types); tests: new `__tests__/messaging-db/message-attempt-fencing.test.ts`, adjusted lock poll in 
`message-create-idempotency.test.ts`.
