   1: # State model
   2: 
   3: ## Current implementation map
   4: 
   5: - PresenceContext composes the subsystem; it is not a second state machine.
   6: - usePresenceSession registers, heartbeats, and disconnects leases through
   7:   /api/presence/sessions.
   8: - usePresenceSnapshot and useUserPresence expose the authoritative,
   9:   company-scoped snapshot.
  10: - usePresenceRealtime listens on a private company topic and only invalidates or
  11:   refetches the snapshot. Realtime payloads do not directly become authority.
  12: - useLocationTransition and the transition coordinator own movement requests.
  13: - useLastSpace may request automatic placement only through that coordinator
  14:   and uses company-and-user-scoped hints.
  15: - /api/presence/location calls the observed atomic location transition.
  16: - /api/users/location remains a gated legacy writer. Never call or extend it;
  17:   new feature movement uses /api/presence/location.
  18: - Browser storage keys must use the vo:presence:<company>:<user>:... namespace.
  19: 
  20: Inspect the relevant source before relying on this map. Reconcile discrepancies
  21: before changing the affected contract; continue independent work meanwhile.
  22: 
  23: ## Authority hierarchy
  24: 
  25: The authoritative snapshot is produced by one database operation at one server
  26: time. It returns the verified viewer identity, company scope, users, spaces,
  27: active session facts, placement/access revisions, and server time needed for
  28: pure derivation. Do not merge independent client queries into an authoritative
  29: snapshot; their read points can differ.
  30: 
  31: Authority, from strongest to weakest:
  32: 
  33: 1. Locked database rows and security-definer transition results.
  34: 2. A validated server snapshot scoped to company ID plus app-user ID.
  35: 3. Query-cache mirrors of that exact snapshot.
  36: 4. Private Realtime invalidations that request a refetch.
  37: 5. Company/user-scoped local-storage hints used only to propose recovery.
  38: 
  39: Realtime payloads, `users.status`, `last_active`, open/closed logs, toasts, and
  40: local clocks never authorize a transition.
  41: 
  42: ## Identity
  43: 
  44: - App user ID is `public.users.id` and owns application foreign keys.
  45: - Auth user ID is `auth.users.id`, mapped through `users.supabase_uid`.
  46: - Auth session ID is the exact server-verified JWT `session_id` claim.
  47: - Company scope is the current locked `users.company_id`, not a body parameter.
  48: 
  49: Every cache, channel, lease-registration request, storage key, and asynchronous
  50: commit is fenced by company ID plus app-user ID. Server registration also
  51: requires the client's expected company and echoes the authoritative company;
  52: any mismatch invalidates the membership scope.
  53: 
  54: ## Placement, connection, and occupancy
  55: 
  56: Placement is persisted intent in `users.current_space_id`. It can survive a
  57: transient disconnect, but it does not prove connection or access.
  58: 
  59: A user is connected only when at least one lease:
  60: 
  61: - belongs to the user, current company, and exact non-revoked auth session;
  62: - has not been retired and is unexpired at snapshot server time; and
  63: - carries the current user access revision.
  64: 
  65: A user occupies a space only when connected and a qualifying lease also:
  66: 
  67: - matches `users.current_space_id` and the lease `space_id`;
  68: - matches `users.location_version` through `placement_version`; and
  69: - matches the current user and space access revisions.
  70: 
  71: Revision mismatch may leave `isConnected=true` while occupancy is false. Never
  72: force the current user into occupancy or capacity when these predicates fail.
  73: 
  74: ## Availability
  75: 
  76: `users.status` stores the preference `online`, `away`, or `busy`. Legacy
  77: `offline` values normalize to `online` for connected users. Display status is:
  78: 
  79: - disconnected: `offline`;
  80: - connected plus `away`: `away`;
  81: - connected plus `busy`: `busy`;
  82: - otherwise connected: `online`.
  83: 
  84: Availability does not create a lease and is not used for authorization,
  85: occupancy, capacity, or responder eligibility.
  86: 
  87: ## Logs and time
  88: 
  89: `space_presence_log` is historical/audit state updated inside atomic movement;
  90: it is not a lease or grace credential. A delayed reconciliation closes a log at
  91: the authoritative disconnect/expiry boundary it proves, not at arbitrary Cron
  92: execution time. Lease comparisons use snapshot/database time, never browser
  93: time.
